# Enumerate Compatible Craft Workflow Futures

> Draft for technical and fluent-language review. The numerical inputs, labels and expected results are authored teaching cases. They are not new physical material tests, native scene runs, learner observations or production outcomes. Human and learner decisions remain undecided.

## Project operation and interpretation

A future craft workflow brief combines detailed embroidery, local generation and operation while offline. Listing each feature independently can produce bundles that violate the brief’s own necessary conditions. Before comparing renderer strategies, construct the scenario space itself. This lesson enumerates every binary bundle under authored compatibility constraints. These are hypothetical requirements for a planning exercise, not claims about current [Blender](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/blender/blender/v4.5.0/README.md), [ComfyUI](https://docs.comfy.org/), [Godot](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/) or BRUTAL capabilities.

Fix the feature order and interpret each implication literally. In this model, detail requires local generation and offline operation also requires local generation. Local generation alone does not promise either feature. Reject a bundle only when its stated condition fails; do not strengthen an implication into equivalence or assume that an unrequired feature must be absent. The retained set is a finite morphology of internally compatible assumptions, with no probability attached to its members.

The control adds a conflict between detail and offline operation. That restriction removes the all-enabled bundle even though each feature can still appear in some compatible bundle separately. It exposes the difference between individual possibility and joint possibility. A future planning agent should bind each constraint to a source or explicit stakeholder premise and retain a reason for every exclusion. Logical consistency remains an early gate: actual adapters, quality, resource limits and authorization need separate evidence before one of these futures becomes an adopted workflow.

Read the committed prerequisite and the scoped primary passage before calculating. Make a small ledger with separate columns for source definition, authored premise, derived result and future observation. A documentation page supports only the claim within its inspected scope. A source parameter, mathematical answer and runtime observation have different evidential roles; an assistant’s confident summary cannot exchange those roles. The evidence packet retains the source revision and the reading boundary so another reviewer can challenge a precise statement.

Work first with the answer panels closed. Draw the table or diagram required by this operation and retain the intermediate quantities, including units or identity conventions. That handwritten derivation is the direct manual baseline. Only then consult an assistant or translation aid. Keep the question, the source location cited, the suggestion received and the change accepted or rejected. Compare the assisted result with the retained first attempt on identical inputs. A shorter answer is not an improvement when it omits a precondition or invents a completed project trial.

