### Exercise 1

Interpret the feature order.

<details><summary>Answer 1</summary>

It is `[detail,local,offline]`. A bitstring must travel with that order; a reordered display cannot silently change its referent.

</details>

### Exercise 2

List the main compatible futures.

<details><summary>Answer 2</summary>

They are `[000,010,011,110,111]`, count `5`. Necessary local generation does not force detail or offline operation.

</details>

### Exercise 3

Explain an excluded bundle.

<details><summary>Answer 3</summary>

Bundle `100` requests detail without local generation and violates its implication. Exclusion records a premise, not an observed product failure.

</details>

### Exercise 4

Apply the added-conflict control.

<details><summary>Answer 4</summary>

Compatible futures become `[000,010,011,110]`, count `4`; `111` is removed. Individual possibility does not establish joint possibility.

</details>

### Exercise 5

May the retained bundles be assigned equal forecast probability?

<details><summary>Answer 5</summary>

No. Enumeration supplies a logical set, not frequencies or justified beliefs. Any probability model needs additional assumptions and evidence.

</details>

## Source-assisted task and direct baseline

Enumerate the bundles on paper before asking an assistant to propose a future craft pipeline. Keep a reason for each rejection and identify which constraints are merely proposed requirements awaiting stakeholder or source confirmation.

Treat the control as a separate input record. Preserve the main case, write a prediction for the changed input and explain which premise changes. When a result disagrees with your first answer, distinguish arithmetic error, interpretation error and a model limitation. Keep a failed attempt beside its correction rather than replacing it. The task asks for a reviewable evidence note before proposing a DSL node or agent workflow; a manual table may already meet the project need.

Submit the baseline, source locations, corrected explanation, control outcome and prospective falsifier together. The prepared criteria below are questions for a future reviewer, not accepted learner results. Actual learner answer, assistance history, corrected answer and learner decision remain empty until a real attempt is retained. Technical review, fluent-language review, runtime execution, production adoption and publication each require their own applicable evidence. A passing finite calculation would establish only the stated operation under its premises.

## Prospective falsifier

A future brief accepting the all-enabled bundle under the added conflict is contradicted by its own joint-compatibility rule.

